	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(20.0, 20.0, 560.0, 82.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">PRAKTIKUM 5 — Features and PCA

PCA REQUIRES SCALING. Run it once with Preprocess in the chain and once
without, and compare the variance explained. That difference is the whole lesson.</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(780.0, 100.0, 330.0, 210.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">WHAT TO DO
1. Rank: which features score highest by information
   gain? Compare with the notebook's mutual info.
2. Preprocess: enable 'Normalize Features'.
3. Open BOTH PCA widgets. How many components
   reach 95% variance in each?
   Scaled: ~? Unscaled: ~1-2. Why?
4. Compare the two scatter plots. The unscaled one
   is essentially a plot of one variable.

See book section 5.6.4, limitation 2.</text>
	</annotations>
